data a_possibly_empty_producer_enters_a_nonempty_consumer: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_possibly_empty_producer_enters_a_nonempty_consumer" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungUnread { cause: FoundAtAmbiguous },

  receipts: [
    "**a possibly-empty producer enters a nonempty consumer** (invalid state: a value whose cardinality lower bound is zero, or unmeasured, reaches a position that requires at least one element. Harm: the operator's canonical seam -- an empty collection into a nonempty consumer -- is a silent wrong answer paid for at runtime or later, DESIGN section 4b's 'floor first, differentiator above it').",

    "Variants that share the cause: a head-and-tail NonEmpty record that restates std.algebra.FreeSemigroup, a validated or nonempty brand constructible without establishing its claimed invariant (a sealed constructor, a type name or an arbitrary predicate callback establishes nothing alone), an operation that preserves a lower bound it can invalidate (filter), and unmeasured cardinality treated as zero or as one.",

    "RECOGNITION RULE: A NONEMPTY CLAIM IS EITHER CONSTRUCTED (FreeSemigroup) OR PROVED AT THE BINDING; A NAME OR A WRAPPER IS NEITHER.",

    "Rung found at: mitigatable / mechanically preventable by individual probes; the in-tree propagation rows are manual value-level specimens. Ceiling: structurally guaranteed for the decidable interval fragment (n..n literals, map preserves, filter floors to 0, concat adds); general refinement predicates stay a ratchet. Next trigger, a capability: binding-level bound propagation judged at a real producer-to-nonempty-consumer seam, delivered by roadmap node `cardinality-vertical-slice` and made Required-blocking by `extended-admission-cardinality`.",

    "EXECUTED READINGS (2026-10-14, quick-newt-81, one path each; rung = the MINIMUM across paths, DESIGN 4b.1). PATH 1, interpreted claims over LOCAL fixture mirrors FsList/FsNonEmpty (v2.test.claim.compiler.free_semigroup_empty_producer_witness): an empty variant at a nonempty-product return and formal refuses; structurally guaranteed for that shape. PATH 2, the BUILT native CLI (generation-one executable of gunbc test //gunbc/instruments:v2-native-cli, `emit --entry` over the live dag root, real `import std.algebra { FreeSemigroup, Empty }`): `fn probe() -> FreeSemigroup<Int> { Empty }` is refused with arrow_body_does_not_inhabit_declared_return, located at the body: an observed refusal, not rung evidence; non-discriminating because the accepted control is unreachable and the same-type generic nullary case (fn f() -> FsList<Int> { FsEmpty }) also refuses. PATH 2 for the `[]` literal at a FreeSemigroup return or formal, and for the constructed positive control, is NOT ESTABLISHED: each refuses resolve_reason_unbound_symbol, and the closure's std.algebra, std.optional and std.unicode.types refuse resolve_reason_parameter_path_not_indexed, the #13832 regression (fn parameters not indexed under an alias type) that #13974 fixes; a refusal that is the same with the control is no reading of the wall. Root cause of why the in-memory fixture closure cannot evidence the literal: `[]` lowers to a reference to std.algebra FreeMonoid (v2.std.list_introduction list_introduction_head_path), and that closure holds only fixture modules; embedding std.algebra text there would be a second authority. compile_dag_diagnostic_census is NOT a route for this class: it is the v1 Rust host (its own doc says so), refuses the literal as InternalError, and emits unclassified rows for both the Empty RED and the control, so it cannot discriminate. Rung: structurally guaranteed only for PATH 1 shapes; the real-corpus FreeSemigroup `[]` seam is below that until #13974 lands and PATH 2 is re-run with the literal and the control. Next trigger: #13974 on main, then re-run the gen-one probe (four modules: `[]` at formal, `Empty` at return, `[]` at return, constructed control) and add the generic alias control.",

    "RUNG PER PATH (2026-10-14, gunbc#13910 landed; the class rung is the MINIMUM across in-scope paths, DESIGN 4b(1)). Three paths. (1) Interpreted v2 fixture path (v2.test.claim.compiler.free_semigroup_empty_producer_witness, local FsList/FsNonEmpty mirrors): an empty producer at a nonempty-product position refuses with a head mismatch from v2.std.inhabitance inhabitance_declaration_heads_differ, with accepted constructed, alias and generic positive controls: structurally guaranteed for the bounded nominal-head shape. (2) Built generation-one native CLI over the real std.algebra: UNESTABLISHED; the one Empty refusal is non-discriminating (see EXECUTED READINGS) and the `[]` literal and the accepted control are unreachable. (3) v1 seed merge path (the ONLY judge on the merge path today): silent -- the seed accepts the same source and nothing refuses, which is BELOW the ladder rather than mitigatable. Path 3 is an unclimbed path, not a rung drop: the seed never held a rung for this class, so gunbc.rung_drop declares nothing and the seed is not edited. The class therefore stands below mitigatable on the merge path, and its minimum below the ladder.",

    "POPULATION: UNMEASURED, NOT ZERO. Executed 2026-10-14 on the generation-one binary kept by `gunbc test //gunbc/instruments:v2-native-cli`, as `emit --entry <e> --source-root src/v2 --source-root dag`. Entry v2.cli.compile_cli: 209 closure members, 207 refused before inhabitance is reached (127 resolve_reason_parameter_path_not_indexed, 64 resolve_reason_unbound_symbol, 6 target_value_expr_reason_transform_shape_invalid, 5 produced_decl_type_ref_unrealized, 5 emit_module_member_*_not_realized or translate_module_not_a_type_expression), 2 accepted. Entry v2.compiler.compile: the whole closure refused, v2.std.integer requested by gunbc.witness.v2_native_route lies in a tree the requesting tree may not import. A zero count of head mismatches over those closures would be vacuous, so none is claimed: the native route cannot judge either closure of gunbc.emitted_subject_build_gate emitted_subject_build_rows. Re-measure when the parameter_path_not_indexed refusals clear (gunbc#13974 is expected to) and update this entry; any instance found is a live defect.",

    "RE-PROBE AFTER #13974 AND #13996 (2026-10-14, tidy-owl-439; a native-binary reading, NOT an enrolled claim, because CI runs only the two emitted closures). Pin c925c9f6a420c4ced40de514d2f0fdd5309b6168; generation-one executable kept by gunbc test //gunbc/instruments:v2-native-cli, binary_sha256 391972753cec9b686dc7229db9811980e9d8c284dbdd316896f6806fbf585363 (re-hashed after the emits, equal), built in one BuildBuddy dispatch with a private CARGO_TARGET_DIR, probes as `emit --entry probe.X --source-root <copy of dag with probe/ added>`. RESULT: THE READING DOES NOT DISCRIMINATE, and the rung of PATH 2 does NOT rise. (a) `[]` at a FreeSemigroup formal and `[]` at a FreeSemigroup return STILL refuse resolve_reason_unbound_symbol at a projected node, so the literal does not get past resolve. (b) `Empty` at a return refuses arrow_body_does_not_inhabit_declared_return at the body, as before. (c) The constructed control `FreeSemigroup { head: 1, tail: Empty }` is REFUSED with record_field_value_does_not_inhabit at the `tail: Empty` value, and the alias-return control refuses the same way, so the accepted control is still unreachable. CAUSE: in every probe std.algebra and std.error_primitives refuse resolve_reason_unbound_symbol and std.optional refuses emit_module_member_generic_not_realized, so the real FreeMonoid/FreeSemigroup declarations are not resolved natively and the control's `tail: Empty` cannot inhabit FreeMonoid<Int>; the same refusal fires with and without the RED, so none of the three REDs is a reading. The #13832 cause is cleared (zero parameter_path_not_indexed), the next wall is unbound_symbol inside std.algebra. The generic alias control was added to the probe set and refuses identically.",

    "POPULATION RE-MEASURED (2026-10-14, same binary and pin as the re-probe; still UNMEASURED, NOT ZERO). Entry v2.cli.compile_cli: parameter_path_not_indexed 0 (was 127); resolve_reason_unbound_symbol 151 (was 64); target_value_expr_reason_transform_shape_invalid 10; infer_reason_projection_receiver_declares_no_fields 3; infer_reason_pattern_payload_formal_uninstantiated 3; target_value_expr_reason_body_scope_binding_invalid 1; resolve_reason_realized_declaration_mismatch 1; arrow_body_does_not_inhabit_declared_return 1 (a head mismatch of one refusal cause; its identity was not located in this reading and is listed as a candidate live defect to attribute, not a counted instance). Entry v2.compiler.compile: refused whole, v2.std.integer requested by gunbc.witness.v2_native_route lies in a tree the requesting tree may not import, unchanged from #13980. The unbound_symbol count rising from 64 to 151 as the earlier wall clears is consistent with modules that were shadowed by parameter_path_not_indexed now reaching resolve; it was not controlled. No head-mismatch count is claimed over either closure.",

    "THE ONE arrow_body_does_not_inhabit_declared_return ATTRIBUTED (2026-10-14, lively-badger-898; a native-binary reading, NOT an enrolled claim, because CI runs only the two emitted closures). Pin 25c8dd6f9772d6997ff9c229e9075bf971f04286; generation-one executable built and kept by gunbc test //gunbc/instruments:v2-native-cli in ONE BuildBuddy dispatch with GITHUB_ACTIONS set to take the CiExempt user-work-scope standing, binary_sha256 1b305ba6b082c13c992ea8e56aa723800440ebf92505c10ca34276e2430539c8 (NOT the 391972753cec... of the earlier reading: a different build of the same instrument, so the refusal count was re-confirmed, not assumed). IDENTITY: `emit --entry v2.cli.compile_cli --source-root src/v2 --source-root dag` refuses exactly one module with this cause, v2.compiler.program_assembly (modules[136]); every other of the closure's refusals is a different cause. SYMBOL: the module's only nullary `Empty` bodies at a declared return are `program_assembly_empty_roots() -> FreeMonoid<NormalizedTree> { Empty }` and `program_assembly_empty_located_roots() -> FreeMonoid<LocatedNormalizedTree> { Empty }`; a copy of the module with both functions deleted (the one caller site of the located one rewritten to `Empty`) no longer refuses with this cause (it refuses infer_reason_projection_receiver_declares_no_fields), so the refusal is one or both of them. Which of the two is NOT split: the diagnostic names the module, not the declaration, and the copy removed both. CLASSIFICATION: NOT a cardinality instance, and NOT an unbound_symbol cascade. Both returns are FreeMonoid, the possibly-empty carrier, so no nonempty position exists (nothing to inhabit a head-and-tail product with); the refusal is the generic-nullary-arm-at-a-declared-return floor defect (fn f() -> FsList<Int> { FsEmpty }), the shape the fixture claim v2.test.claim.compiler.free_semigroup_empty_producer_witness already notes. DISCRIMINATING CONTROLS, same binary, probe root a copy of dag plus probe/ with src/v2 beside it: probe.p1 (local `type FsList<T> = FsEmpty | FsCons {...}`, `fn f() -> FsList<Int> { FsEmpty }`, NO std.algebra import) REFUSES arrow_body_does_not_inhabit_declared_return, so the cause needs neither std.algebra nor unbound_symbol; probe.p5 (the real std.algebra FreeMonoid<Int> with `Empty`) refuses the same; probe.p4 (local nonempty product, `FsEmpty` at its return) refuses the same, so this cause cannot tell a real empty-into-nonempty from a possibly-empty return and is not a reading of the class; probe.p3 (local generic, constructed `FsCons { head: 1, tail: FsEmpty }` at the same return) and probe.p2 (non-generic nullary at a return) do NOT refuse with this cause (they reach emit and stop at emit_module_member_generic_not_realized and target_value_expr_reason_transform_shape_invalid), so the refusal is specific to a generic coproduct's nullary arm at a return. VERDICT: no live instance of this class in the compile_cli closure, and the rung of PATH 2 does NOT rise (p4 versus p1 is indistinguishable). The nonempty-vs-possibly-empty distinction needs the floor defect repaired first so that p1 is accepted and p4 stays refused; that repair is owned by royal-raven-317 (not landed at this pin) and is not made here.",

    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, a capability: the native route resolves and judges the self-host and native-cli closures, and the native inhabitance check judges the required merge path -- the same capability as gunbc.rung_drop v2_native_route_off_the_merge_path, whose trigger this shares. Until then the seed route stays silent for this class.",
    "PROOF-CARRYING CONVERSION, BLOCKED ON A LANGUAGE CAPABILITY (2026-10-14, #13994 frontier; ruling nonemptiness_is_constructed_or_proved). A FreeMonoid proved nonempty reaches a FreeSemigroup position only through a named conversion nonempty_by_proof<T>(xs: FreeMonoid<T>) -> FreeSemigroup<T> whose call infer would judge (PLANNED, none of this exists yet: an expression-count fold over v2.std.cardinality CardinalityConstraint and cardinality_operation_laws; proved -> accepted, known-unproved -> refused, unknown count -> refused rather than undecidable-accepted, with typed reasons to be named when the judgment is built). The three seams and declared_type_inhabitance stay unchanged, because implicit admission on a proof is forbidden by DESIGN 4. The eliminator trigger is DISCHARGED (gunbc#14022): Never now lives in the import-free std.error_primitives module with no producer, and absurd<T>(n: Never) -> T is the generic eliminator (an empty match is exhaustive only for that Never, keyed on DeclarationRef identity, and the v2 empty match is admitted only as an arrow body). The Empty arm of nonempty_by_proof is therefore still not writable, but no longer for want of an eliminator: it needs a Never VALUE, which the arm cannot obtain without narrowing xs by the count proof (a refinement of the scrutinee), which the checker does not carry. A self-call breaks bounded execution and a fabricated head is a DESIGN 5 fabricated default; no realization-binding mechanism exists for a bodiless pure fn. TRIGGER, ONE capability, no second bottom type: the checker narrowing a scrutinee by a proved cardinality so that the Empty arm is judged unreachable, i.e. holds a Never value; with it, nonempty_by_proof is an ordinary total body over absurd. Consumer of the cardinality carrier and count laws until then: none in production (declared frontier of DESIGN 3c); the judgment, its fold and its reason symbols are design, not authority.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.compiler.free_semigroup_empty_producer_witness", decl_name: "fse_empty_at_a_declared_free_semigroup_return_refuses_holds", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.compiler.free_semigroup_empty_producer_witness", decl_name: "fse_empty_variant_at_a_nonempty_product_formal_refuses_holds", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.compiler.free_semigroup_empty_producer_witness", decl_name: "fse_a_constructed_nonempty_value_is_accepted_holds", field: WholeDeclaration },
